{
  "schema_version": "optical-design-task.tmm.v1",
  "task_id": "tmm_design_a_22_layer_alternating_tio2_sio2_dielectr_b605c0b836",
  "user_request_original": "Design a 22-layer alternating TiO2/SiO2 dielectric stack on fused silica substrate at 45 degrees incidence. Initialize all layers at quarter-wave optical thickness centered at 550nm (TiO2 approximately 57nm, SiO2 approximately 96nm based on typical indices). Set thickness bounds 30-250nm for all layers. Execute staged gradient optimization: first optimize only outermost 6 layers (layers 1-3 and 20-22) while holding inner 16 layers fixed at quarter-wave values; second stage optimize layers 1-10 and 13-22 holding layers 11-12 fixed; final stage optimize all 22 layers. Target observable: maximize weighted sum of mean reflectance in 450-650nm band and mean transmittance in 700-1000nm band. Incident medium is air. Evaluate both s and p polarization states and report unpolarized average. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 450-650 nm, 700-1000 nm. soft objectives: high reflectance in 450-650 nm; high transmittance in 700-1000 nm; minimized crosstalk between bands. behaviors to suppress or avoid: transmittance in 450-650 nm; reflectance in 700-1000 nm. manufacturing constraints: maximum 24 layers.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Design and optimize a 22-layer alternating TiO2/SiO2 dielectric stack on a fused-silica substrate at 45-degree incidence. Initialize all coating layers at quarter-wave optical thickness for a 550 nm center wavelength with thickness bounds of 30–250 nm. Execute a three-stage gradient optimization: first activate layers 1–3 and 20–22, then layers 1–10 and 13–22, finally all 22 layers. Optimize for high reflectance in the 450–650 nm band and high transmittance in the 700–1000 nm band, while minimizing transmission in the first band and reflection in the second. Evaluate at 45 deg incidence for s and p polarizations and unpolarized light.",
